    <p class="lede first reveal">Somewhere on your phone is a list. Product ideas, half of them good, none of them made. You have been circling the same question for months: what should my first digital product be? And every answer sends you back to research instead of forward to a file that exists.</p>
    <p class="reveal">Here is what no one tells you at the start. The question is not which product is best. It is which one you will actually finish. A perfect product that lives in your head earns nothing. A modest one that exists can earn for years.</p>
    <p class="reveal"><strong>You do not have an ideas problem. You have a finishing problem.</strong> A digital product is just a specific promise, delivered as a file. Once you stop hunting for the perfect idea and start shipping a real one, the whole thing gets unstuck.</p>

