    <div class="chapter left reveal"><span class="bignum">02</span><div class="num">Chapter Two</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="exist">Why the first one is about existing, not being good</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">Your first digital product's only job is to exist and get in front of one buyer. The feedback from one real sale teaches you more than another month of polishing ever will.</p>
    <p class="reveal">Perfectionism is procrastination in a nicer outfit. The women stuck at zero are almost never the ones with bad ideas — they're the ones refining a good idea into a product that never ships. <strong>You cannot improve a thing that doesn't exist.</strong> Version one exists so version two can be smart.</p>

    <div class="photo-quote reveal">
