    <div class="chapter left reveal"><span class="bignum">06</span><div class="num">Chapter Six</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="sell">Selling it before anyone knows you</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">You sell your first product without an audience by putting it where people are already searching — Pinterest and your own content — so strangers find the product through the problem it solves, not through you.</p>
    <p class="reveal">This is the whole advantage of the faceless model. You are not waiting for a following to trust your face. You are answering a question someone is already typing, and your product is the answer. <strong>A pin pointing at a real solution works whether you have ten followers or ten thousand.</strong></p>

