    <div class="chapter reveal"><span class="bignum">07</span><div class="num">Chapter Seven</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="repeat">What turns one product into income that repeats</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">One product becomes repeating income when you stop rebuilding from scratch — a shelf of related products, or a subscription that refreshes, turns a single sale into a system that compounds.</p>
    <p class="reveal">The first sale proves the model. The system is what makes it a business. Once you know a product sells, the smart move isn't a wildly different second product — it's a related one for the same buyer, or a way to keep delivering to her over time.</p>

