    <div class="chapter reveal"><div class="num">Answered</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="faq">Frequently asked</h2></div>
    <h3 class="reveal">What is the best digital product to sell as a beginner?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">A template, planner, or short guide that solves one specific problem you already understand. The "best" one is the one you can finish this week and clearly describe in a sentence — not the most ambitious idea on your list.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">How do I price my first digital product?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Start with a price you can say out loud without flinching — often somewhere between five and twenty-seven dollars for a first product. Price for the outcome it delivers, not the number of pages. You can always raise it once it's selling.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">Can I really sell without a big following?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Yes, and it's the whole point of a faceless business. When your product is found through search — Pinterest, your own articles — buyers arrive because they have the problem, not because they follow you. The audience is nice later; it isn't the requirement to start.</p>

